@title INC-3302: Late nightly sales reports
@subtitle Postmortem for the 2026-10-06 incident at Marrow Retail
@author Data Platform team, Owner
@date 2026-10-06

kpi Reports late | 8 h 40 min | due 03:00, sent 11:40 | bad
kpi Store managers affected | 214 | empty or stale reports | bad
kpi Backfill time | 95 min | serial run | neutral

# Summary
The point-of-sale vendor added a column named `tender_subtype` to the sales feed without notice, and the ingestion job failed on it. The failure alert went to a retired channel, so nobody knew until a store manager asked why the report was empty. Reports due at 03:00 UTC were published at 11:40 UTC.

# Timeline
table = Time (UTC),Event; 01:15,Vendor deploys the schema change; 02:10,Ingestion job fails for the first time; 02:40,Retries exhausted; 03:00,**Reports miss their deadline, no alert fires**; 07:25,A store manager asks in #retail-ops why the report is empty; 07:50,Support pages the Data Platform on-call; 08:35,Cause identified; 09:20,Schema mapping patched; 10:05,Backfill starts; 11:40,Reports published

# Contributing factors
- Pipeline failure alerts still routed to the retired channel #data-alerts-old.
- There was no schema contract check on vendor feeds, so an unannounced column broke ingestion.
- The backfill ran serially, which stretched recovery to 95 min.

# What went well
- Once paged, the on-call found the cause in 45 min.
- No wrong numbers were published.

# Action items
table = Action,Owner,Due; Route pipeline alerts to the on-call pager,Samuel Achterberg,2026-10-16; Require 14 days' notice of feed changes in the vendor contract,Vendor Management,2026-10-30; Add a schema contract check on vendor feeds,Lucia Fontaine,2026-11-06; Parallelize the backfill by partition,Data Platform on-call,2026-11-20
